  Stacks.CohenMacaulayTensor.solution k K L h


/-!
# Cohen–Macaulayness is insensitive to a finitely generated field extension of the base

Proof of Stacks 045N: for `k` a field, `S` a Noetherian `k`-algebra, `K/k` a finitely generated
field extension, `𝔮 ⊆ S` a prime and `𝔮_K ⊆ K ⊗[k] S` a prime lying over it, the local ring
`S_𝔮` is Cohen–Macaulay if and only if `(K ⊗[k] S)_{𝔮_K}` is.

The two localisations are abstract, so the first step replaces them by the canonical models
`Localization.AtPrime`; Cohen–Macaulayness of a local ring only depends on its isomorphism class.
For the canonical models, `S_𝔮 → (S_K)_{𝔮_K}` is a flat local homomorphism of Noetherian local
rings: `K ⊗[k] S` is Noetherian because it is essentially of finite type over `S` (Stacks 045I),
and it is flat over `S` because `K` is flat over the field `k`. Its fibre
`(S_K)_{𝔮_K} / 𝔮 (S_K)_{𝔮_K}` is a localisation of the fibre ring
`κ(𝔮) ⊗[S] (K ⊗[k] S) ≅ κ(𝔮) ⊗[k] K`, which is Cohen–Macaulay by Stacks 045M since `K/k` is
finitely generated. So the fibre condition in Stacks 045J holds unconditionally and that lemma
reduces to the desired equivalence.

## Main results

* `Stacks.CohenMacaulay.BaseFieldExtension.solution`: Stacks 045N.

## Implementation notes

The mathematics of the fibre step is `depth_eq_ringKrullDim_of_isCohenMacaulay_fiber`: for a prime
`𝔯 ⊆ T` lying over `𝔮 ⊆ S`, the fibre `T_𝔯 / 𝔮 T_𝔯` of `S_𝔮 → T_𝔯` is the localisation of the
fibre ring `κ(𝔮) ⊗[S] T` at the prime corresponding to `𝔯` under
`PrimeSpectrum.primesOverOrderIsoFiber`, the identification being Mathlib's
`Ideal.Fiber.algEquivAux₂`. In particular the fibre is a Cohen–Macaulay local ring whenever the
fibre ring is a Cohen–Macaulay ring, which is where Stacks 045M enters. That identification
presents the fibre as a quotient by `𝔮 T_𝔯` while the fibre condition of Stacks 045J is phrased
with `𝔪_{S_𝔮} T_𝔯`; the two ideals agree by `map_maximalIdeal_eq_map_of_liesOver`.

All the bookkeeping with depth is carried by `depth_eq_depth_map`: depth is transported along a
surjective ring map `f : A →+* B` together with an additive equivalence `M ≃+ N` intertwining the
actions. That covers both the invariance of self-depth under a ring isomorphism and the passage
between the depth of `B ⧸ I` over `B` and its depth over `B ⧸ I` itself; the latter is needed
because the fibre condition of Stacks 045J is an equation between a depth over `T_𝔯` and a Krull
dimension, whereas Cohen–Macaulayness of the local ring `T_𝔯 / 𝔮 T_𝔯` is an equation of invariants
of that ring.

The `S`-algebra structure on `K ⊗[k] S` is `Algebra.TensorProduct.rightAlgebra` and the
`S_𝔮`-algebra structure on `(S_K)_{𝔮_K}` is `Localization.AtPrime.algebraOfLiesOver`, both local
instances here; neither is global in Mathlib, the first because it clashes with the left structure
and the second to avoid a diamond over `Ideal.Fiber`. That diamond is why the fibre step goes
through the `S`-algebra form `Ideal.Fiber.algEquivAux₂` rather than the `S_𝔮`-algebra form
`Ideal.Fiber.localizationAlgEquivQuotient`, whose `Algebra S_𝔮 T_𝔯` instance argument is the one
`Ideal.Fiber` already carries and not the local instance used here.

